 it  was quite complicated and I remember it  being absolutely annoying and terrible  to make but it was really fun trying to  figure out how these things look exactly  and how to remodel them in step and get  them in the game and get them to work  somehow if you're interested in seeing  parts of that's I do have a video on my  channel of clumsy tiger which is an old  inverted coaster that I made in roller  coaster tycoon 3 which has a cable car  video as well and I'll link that down in  the description as well just in case  you're interested now finally I did copy  the station of  the the welder what would you call it  the valley station over unto the the  peak of the chairlifts here but I did  want to add something else to it so  here's the cabin where the operator is  going to sit and operate the ride that's  just part of realism something that I  didn't want to miss but I'm definitely  not going to dress these things up like  it's some kind of themed parts of the  theme park or whatever I'm really going  to keep this very strictly technical and  as simple as possible especially with a  lot of these modern the chair lifts  you'll just see that they're basically  limited to the bare minimum in terms of  architecture needed to keep these things  running see how this is all quite simple  although I do have to say I kind of do  like the look of this station I had to  take some time to get used to it and you  might also notice that I messed with it  a little bit the glass is less tall now  and the station as a whole is much more  flat looking but I think it's a decent  look although that said in the next  episode I do want to work on some very  different station designs anyway moving  on from there I'm placing a lot of trees  in this area to basically mark outs that  little path which is going to be a blue  slope which i think is quite important  because the the general slopes of this  hill are quite steep so there's really  not there's really no way to make a  natural blue slope here but what you're  very often find at ski resorts is that  they'll use roads leaning up the  mountains as slopes or pastes Oh God  in in winter months to try and have some  kind of beginner feasts in case that the  mountain is very rough and in case the  terrain doesn't really allow for easier  slopes so that's something that I wanted  to have go up the hill as well not to  mention that it very well connects the  three different pieces that we could  have going down the mountain as well so  I think that's a nice touch also and  to be very honest I think ski resorts  also kind of use these things to cheat  on the number of slopes they have or the  length of slopes they have not really  cheats but it's kind of like Lick Bates  you know very often ski resorts will  advertise that they have 70 kilometres  of piste or 50 kilometres of piste and  you know it's not really representative  of whether these are wide groomed slopes  or whether these are just little paths  running through the forests on and on I  remember a ski resort in Japan that I've  been to where you could go down the  entire mountain on this one little slope  that was basically just a road leading  to the top of the mountain you couldn't  even get off of it and go to like  regular piste slopes oh my god it's you  just had to stay on this little path I  believe that was somewhere on Bondi  Mountain I don't think it was the entire  length of the mountain but it was  definitely the longest little path  through the forests that I've ever taken  on skis although at the same time I also  really liked these things you know  there's something to having a variety of  different piste other resorts I really  like very wide and straight pieces but  also these little paths through the  forest  especially on your first go through them  are just a really nice kind of  adventurous explorative little you know  look into nature and the general area  which is really nice I mean at the end  of the day for me especially as a Dutch  person it's really cool to go skiing  because you're in the mountains you're  in a region where there are actually  elevation differences and that alone  just makes exploring it and looking  around you so much cooler although I'm  pretty sure that for pretty much  everybody the views and the overall  nature is just a really big thrall to  skiing as well now here I'm working on  some of the other mountains which I  won't work on yet in this video but I  just wanted to shape them out to get an  idea of what I wanted these things to be  shaped like but as you can see it's  difficult to make these hills with very  small brushes that we have in planet  coaster at least it's manageable though  and with a lot of smoothing you can get  some decent sand and smooth hills as  well so that's not too bad but yeah I'm  gonna probably build a big gondola to  the top of this hill right here and then  some kind of smaller ski lifts to the  other one whatever happens we'll see in  the next episode so yeah thanks for  watching guys and see you guys next time  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

